Mentari was built for Build Before Q-Day: The QoreChain Developer Fest.

This product follows patterns from the QoreChain workshop examples:

  qorechain/build-before-qday
  https://github.com/qorechain/build-before-qday
  Copyright 2026 QoreChain
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

  - workshop-2/01-qday-vault (pqcVerify and pqcKeyStatus calls, ML-DSA-87 signing script)
  - workshop-3/02-cross-vm (EVM-to-Native call through the Cross-VM bridge)

Where code is adapted from these examples, the source file says so in a
header comment.

Third-party packages (for example the QoreChain kits under @qorechain/*,
Foundry's forge-std, Vite, React, vitest and Playwright) keep their own
licences. They are listed with their versions in package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml
and .gitmodules, and credited in README.md.

Fonts: Bricolage Grotesque, Instrument Sans and IBM Plex Mono, each under the
SIL Open Font License 1.1. The site loads them from Fontsource packages; the
slides embed them from deck/fonts/, next to their licence files.
